  "comment": "NINETEENTH PACK. Tamil: an ABUGIDA like Devanagari but with its own marks, declared with NO segmentation override — it writes with spaces, and the space is the truth about it. So the pack is a clean second witness for the law that a combining mark is a letter by office: if the law holds, Tamil passes by the space with no instrument edit at all. It also carries a person the engine cannot hold: INCLUSIVE நாம் and EXCLUSIVE நாங்கள் are two different meanings of «we», so the language has SEVEN persons and the forge crashes on the seventh (IndexError, langpack_forge.py:86). Six are declared and the inclusive is lost, named here rather than faked. Verbs are stem+ending and DO take the pack's rule — weak -கிற- against strong -க்கிற-. TIER 1.",
